# Where this interpreter and the specification differ, and what is to
# become of each difference. A difference the guard can find and this
# list does not name is a failure; so is a line here naming a difference
# the guard can no longer find.
#
# This half was missing. The family had a membership half here and a
# behavioural half in tests/filter_family_test.ps, and the one deviation
# either had found was asserted there and recorded nowhere a reader of
# this file would meet it. A register whose differences live in another
# file tells a reader the family has none.
#
#   <what>  <settled|thorn|heading>  <reason>

ccittfax-eats-the-sentinel  thorn  Five of the six round-trippable decoders stop at their own end-of-data and leave what follows for the next reader. CCITTFaxDecode does not: it never recognises its end-of-block marker, stops only by running out of input, and decodes whatever was written after the marker as a further row -- reporting it damaged and consuming it. Task #330 carries the measurement. It is the same class as the lazy end-of-data desynchronisation that was found in all five stream decoders and fixed there; this one was not in that fix because it was not in that family of five. What removes it is the decoder recognising its own end-of-block marker and stopping there, as the other five stop at theirs; the cost is that the marker is optional in the encoding, so the decoder must still stop on running out of input and the two conditions have to agree. tests/filter_family_test.ps holds it to the WRONG answer with the task named, so the day it is fixed that test fails and asks to be made strict; this line is the same fact where a reader of the register will find it


